                    <mxGeometry x="1021.25" y="348" width="132.5" height="150" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="32" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;What it all means?&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: center; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;In the orchestration_layer.py we define the class Conductor() class. This class will be used by the main.py module for initializing the conductor object which has the useful start() and stop() methods inherited from the Conductor() class. This means we import orchestration_layer.py in the start of main.py file.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#000000&quot;&gt;As defined in the orchestration_layer.py / Conductor(), the conductor object can:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: rgb(63, 63, 63); text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: rgb(63, 63, 63); text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;initialize all the objects, pass the queues and stop signals to the object constructors so the objects know where to get their data and when to stop executing their main loops and finally defining the threads to run each objects&#39; main loop method and defining the way to stop threads.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0); text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;For example capture_layer.py holds the definition for the FrameCapturer() class. FrameCapturer() class tells what the capturer object can do - capture frames from the camera stream essential for our image processing. This class is brought from the capture_layer.py module to the orchestrator_layer.py module this way:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0); text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0); text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0); text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0); text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0); text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0); text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0); text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0); text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0); text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0); text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0); text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0); text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;When the conductor object is initialized this constructor will be called. The constructor here is incomplete because you might want to add more queues here. The constructor defines attributes for the conductor object such as frame_queue and stop_event flag for stopping threads. The constructor also defines capturer attribute which is the capturer object we talked about previously. For the capturer object&#39;s constructor it gives two queues and one stop_event variable. These will be used by the capturer object to send the captured frames to the frame_queue and in the future to the frame_store_queue perhaps. The stop_event variable will be used to turn off the capturer object&#39;s main loop that captures frames and sends them down these queues:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;Next in the Conductor() class is the start method for the conductor object. This is the famous conductor.start() the main.py calls in the entry to the software. Here you can add all the concurrent threads you want to start in a list. It goes through the list and starts every thread starting from the thread that will hold the capturer object and its get_frame method as its target. This means that capturer.get_frame method will be run on a new thread. If we take a look inside capture_layer that holds the information on this object&#39;s class we can see from the get_frame() method that it has loop that captures frames and sends them down on the queues we talked about previously. This means capturer object is just invidual player deciding about it&#39;s own things in the orchestra the conductor conducts. The role of the conductor is to just coordinate the orchestra:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;When the conductor is told by main.py to stop, this part of the conductor is run as defined in the Conductor() class:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;The stop_event will be set which means the stop_event will get value true. Because this variable was passed to the capturer object when it was initialized, the capturer&#39;s attribute stop_event will also get assigned the value true. Because capturer&#39;s main loop/method get_frame() has&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&quot;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: Consolas, &amp;quot;Courier New&amp;quot;, monospace; font-size: 14px; white-space: pre; color: rgb(203, 166, 247); font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;while&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(205, 214, 244); font-family: Consolas, &amp;quot;Courier New&amp;quot;, monospace; font-size: 14px; white-space: pre;&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: Consolas, &amp;quot;Courier New&amp;quot;, monospace; font-size: 14px; white-space: pre; color: rgb(137, 220, 235); font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;not&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(205, 214, 244); font-family: Consolas, &amp;quot;Courier New&amp;quot;, monospace; font-size: 14px; white-space: pre;&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: Consolas, &amp;quot;Courier New&amp;quot;, monospace; font-size: 14px; white-space: pre; color: rgb(250, 179, 135);&quot;&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(205, 214, 244); font-family: Consolas, &amp;quot;Courier New&amp;quot;, monospace; font-size: 14px; white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;.stop_event.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: Consolas, &amp;quot;Courier New&amp;quot;, monospace; font-size: 14px; white-space: pre; color: rgb(137, 180, 250); font-style: italic;&quot;&gt;is_set&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(205, 214, 244); font-family: Consolas, &amp;quot;Courier New&amp;quot;, monospace; font-size: 14px; white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;():&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(205, 214, 244); font-size: 14px; white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&quot;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px; white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;the capturer object&#39;s get_frame will stop and&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px; white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;thus the thread that targeted that method&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px; white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;will do nothing for awhile until the thread &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px; white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;will be told to join.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(63, 63, 63); font-size: 14px; white-space: pre; font-family: Verdana; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt; thread.join() means:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 8px 0px; color: rgb(205, 214, 244); font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe WPC&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; background-color: rgb(24, 24, 37);&quot;&gt;Wait until the thread terminates.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 8px 0px; color: rgb(205, 214, 244); font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe WPC&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; background-color: rgb(24, 24, 37);&quot;&gt;This blocks the calling thread until the thread whose join() method is&lt;br&gt;called terminates -- either normally or through an unhandled exception&lt;br&gt;or until the optional timeout occurs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="1275" y="360" width="330" height="2330" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="33" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;How to run it?&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;Currently if you run this software from the main.py module (the entry point to the entire software) it will probably crash because detection_layer.py, tracking_layer.py, world_state_layer.py and visualization_layer.py and game_logic_layer.py&amp;nbsp; are undefined.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;For first run its enough if you finish detection, tracking, world_state and visualization_layer.py. Keep in mind that you need to define the queues between these layers because they will be run concurrently. Also visualization_layer needs a frame from the capturer object so be prepared to touch capture_layer.py to define the queue for this.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;shadow=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="1275" y="40" width="280" height="340" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="34" value="" style="shape=image;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;labelBackgroundColor=default;verticalAlign=top;aspect=fixed;imageAspect=0;image=data:image/png,;" vertex="1" parent="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="1275" y="780" width="642.48" height="300" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="36" value="" style="shape=flexArrow;endArrow=classic;html=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="6" target="25">
                    <mxGeometry width="50" height="50" relative="1" as="geometry">
                        <mxPoint x="530" y="280" as="sourcePoint"/>
                        <mxPoint x="580" y="230" as="targetPoint"/>
                    </mxGeometry>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="37" value="&lt;pre&gt;&lt;b&gt;try:&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;conductor.start()&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;while True:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;time.sleep(1)&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;except KeyboardInterrupt:&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;print(&quot;stopping&quot;)&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;conductor.stop()&lt;/pre&gt;" style="edgeLabel;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];" vertex="1" connectable="0" parent="36">
                    <mxGeometry x="-0.4128" y="-1" relative="1" as="geometry">
                        <mxPoint x="41" y="40" as="offset"/>
                    </mxGeometry>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="38" value="&lt;p style=&quot;color: rgb(63, 63, 63); scrollbar-color: rgb(226, 226, 226) rgb(251, 251, 251); text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;scrollbar-color: rgb(226, 226, 226) rgb(251, 251, 251); font-weight: 700; text-align: center; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;conductor.start() runs these threads. Each thread runs the main loop method of the object the thread is assigned with.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;color: rgb(63, 63, 63); scrollbar-color: rgb(226, 226, 226) rgb(251, 251, 251); text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;scrollbar-color: rgb(226, 226, 226) rgb(251, 251, 251); font-weight: 700; text-align: center; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;You can observe the thread definitions and start() method of the conductor object from the orchestration_layer.py module.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;color: rgb(63, 63, 63); scrollbar-color: rgb(226, 226, 226) rgb(251, 251, 251); text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;scrollbar-color: rgb(226, 226, 226) rgb(251, 251, 251); font-weight: 700; text-align: center; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;Threads (in practice) mean &quot;run two scripts simultaneously/concurrently&quot;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;color: rgb(63, 63, 63); scrollbar-color: rgb(226, 226, 226) rgb(251, 251, 251); text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;scrollbar-color: rgb(226, 226, 226) rgb(251, 251, 251); font-weight: 700; text-align: center; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;Queues are used here to transfer data from object to another object which in this case also mean from thread to thread since objects and their main loop methods are run on threads&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: rgb(63, 63, 63); font-weight: 700; text-align: center;&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="270" y="90" width="250" height="180" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="39" value="" style="shape=image;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;labelBackgroundColor=default;verticalAlign=top;aspect=fixed;imageAspect=0;image=data:image/png,;" vertex="1" parent="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="1275.89" y="1330" width="641.59" height="220" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="40" value="" style="shape=image;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;labelBackgroundColor=default;verticalAlign=top;aspect=fixed;imageAspect=0;image=data:image/png,;" vertex="1" parent="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="1275" y="1860" width="640" height="173.78" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="41" value="" style="shape=image;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;labelBackgroundColor=default;verticalAlign=top;aspect=fixed;imageAspect=0;image=data:image/png,;" vertex="1" parent="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="1275" y="2130" width="640" height="176.37" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
            </root>
        </mxGraphModel>
    </diagram>
</mxfile>